ans how many new women do you  have well we have two right now one is  young Kim who was born in South Korea  she's a leading in the polls and this is  a real this is a challenge we had  because a number of our women ran for  higher office and moved out and it was  the year of the woman if you look at the  Democrats a Republican Party no it  wasn't a much we have we have room for  but if you look at in the Democratic  primaries where there was an open seat  and it was a woman versus a man a woman  won 69 percent of the time so of course  they had more women coming forward we  can do better in recruitment and that's  what I'm excited about doing but also  look at who else is coming in as  freshmen Republicans if you look Dan  Crenshaw a veteran working on that  service if you look at Mike Waltz the  first Green Beret officer we're diverse  but we continue to expand and improve it  one thing about my leadership is  constant improvement that's good we  could all use constant improvement join  you on that but let's talk about the  diversity issue too because they had a  very interesting picture congressman the  other day on the Republican side it  seemed to be a lot of white guys in  suits on the Republican side on the  Democratic side on the Republican side a  lot of white guys in suits on the  Democratic side you saw women you saw  people of color are you worried about  diversity too is that another area so it  looks and we need to improve on that too  yeah we had a number of people who had  lost seats that would fit in different  categories like that Carlos Cabello and  others we didn't win in the in some of  these seats and I look at improvement I  look at an ability to move forward and  that is one area will continue to work  forward on congressman one of the things  we hear from women and minorities is  that they were turned off by the  president's rhetoric his tone you had a  good working relationship with the  president in fact it was noted that at  times you bring him starbursts what if  anything Jerry and Jerry and  strawberries in particular why did what  can you tell him about his rhetoric and  what needs to be changed look tone  matters a lot where we're going but I  think would happen and you watched it in  that presidential election in campaigns  people battle and I think people were  getting frustrated on both sides of the  aisle if you watched in the last  presidential election for Republican to  Democrat I want someone who would fight  through and they made a decision and the  president hasn't changed from who he was  as a candidate to who he is today but I  think there's always a way to bring more  people together I look at what happened  in the White House yesterday you look at  the bipartisanship that happen for  criminal justice reform now a lot of  people have tried to do that pass  administration's have tried to do that  we're on the brink of making that happen  we passed it in the house and when I  looked in the Senate yesterday it made  all criteria of what you're asking me  about sitting inside the White House  with President Trump as president making  this happen getting through the Senate  yeah hang out that'll come back and  become law so yes there's places for  improvement but there's also places he's  been very successful in and I look at  the final part of the results yes  Oh leader McCarthy I understand that you  have interviewed at the White House with  the president for the job of White House  chief of staff would you take that job  you know I have not interviewed for that  job and I have a job I was just elected  to look I have a focus our number-one  goal here is to make sure we move  America Forward I will work with anyone  who wants to work to make America better  I have a second job as becoming the  Republican leader to win that majority  back and I'm focused on that and that  will be my job in the next and that  includes working with Nancy Pelosi if  she is a fact speaker yeah whoever  becomes Speaker I can work on the other  side of the aisle with them any place  that we can find improvement but we have  to remember to when elections are over  we should govern if the agenda is just  gonna be investigations mhm I think  America is too great for such a small  vision let's think about how do we make  America than the next century ours what  are we doing about prospered solving our  veterans problem we did well combating  opioids with our bill bipartisan what we  did to transform and stop human  trafficking online we're just doing  criminal justice there are a lot of  places we can work together let's put  those things that divide as a side and  you talk about this a more perfect union  we have an opportunity this is an  exceptional country America will always  be the greatest when we find our places  that we can work together and make sure  the next century is ours well you need  to spread that word to some of your  colleagues I know the president calls  you Mike Evan of all the nicknames that  he's come up with Mike Evan sounds  pretty good Mike Evans all right with me  all right  you bye Mike Evan

